          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-10-16 17:54:59.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20978 lnet: use current transaction_timeout for responses",
        "message": "LU-20978 lnet: use current transaction_timeout for responses\n\nThe monitor thread checks for expired responses every\ntransaction_timeout / 2 seconds. It caches the time of the next\ncheck. With the default of 150 s, the next check can be 75 s away.\nA lower transaction_timeout does not move that check. After\n\"lnetctl set transaction_timeout 10\", a lost REPLY expires after\nup to 75 s, not after 10 to 15 s.\n\nKeep the time of the last check. Compare it to the current\ntransaction_timeout on each pass of the monitor thread.\n\nsanity-lnet test_243 loses one REPLY after it sets\ntransaction_timeout to 10:\n\n    without the fix: ping fails after 72 s\n    with the fix:    ping fails after 13 to 14 s\n\nFixes: dc1f5f08b420 (\"LU-11468 lnet: configure recovery interval\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lnet env=ONLY=243,ONLY_REPEAT=10\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5\nChange-Id: I91c78dbc9c69215836420a5fc00e2a0803ca42e9\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
